### ============================================================
### 1 — No session
### Run these before logging in
### ============================================================

### Health check, open endpoint
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Current user without a session, expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Wrong password, expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123X"}

### Disabled account, expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "avi", "password": "password123"}


### ============================================================
### 2 — Manager session
### ============================================================

### Login as manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana", "password": "password123"}

### Current user, expect 200 MANAGER
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Manager endpoint, expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/manager-only

### --- Job positions ---

### List positions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions

### Create position
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Team lead"}

### Duplicate name, expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Support agent"}

### Empty name, expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": ""}

### Delete position in use, expect 409
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions/1

### Not found, expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions/999

### --- Shift types ---

### List shift types
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types

### Create a shift crossing midnight
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Late night", "startTime": "22:00", "endTime": "06:00"}

### Same start and end, expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Broken", "startTime": "08:00", "endTime": "08:00"}

### --- Employees ---

### List employees
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### Create employee
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Roni Katz", "username": "roni", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### Duplicate username, expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Fake", "username": "maya", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### Non-existent job position, expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Ghost", "username": "ghost", "password": "password123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 999}

### Short password, expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName": "Short", "username": "shorty", "password": "123",
  "role": "EMPLOYEE", "maxWeeklyHours": 40, "jobPositionId": 2}

### Deactivate the only manager, expect 400
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/1


### ============================================================
### 3 — Employee session
### Logging in as an employee replaces the manager cookie
### ============================================================

### Login as employee
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "maya", "password": "password123"}

### Current user, expect 200 EMPLOYEE
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Employee endpoint, expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/employee-only

### Manager endpoint, expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/debug/manager-only

### List employees, expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees

### Create position, expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Hacker"}

### Create shift type, expect 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-types
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nope", "startTime": "10:00", "endTime": "18:00"}


### ============================================================
### 4 — Logout
### ============================================================

### Log out, expect 204
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout

### Current user after logout, expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Protected endpoint after logout, expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-positions


### ============================================================
### 5 — Employee created through the API can log in
### ============================================================

### Login as the employee created above
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "roni", "password": "password123"}

### Current user, expect 200 with employeeId of roni
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Log out
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout
